{
  "why": [
    "Backlog row 13 of docs/audits/2026-10-03-frontend-design-system-audit.md:",
    "  \"every one of the 35 pages gets four states (loading / empty / error+retry / success) as a checklist item\".",
    "One entry per file in frontend/src/pages, four states each, with the evidence the scanner can see:",
    "  kind \"notice\"  - a rendered block that states the state (the shared components/ui/DataState set, or the page's own);",
    "  kind \"inline\"  - the state is rendered inside the page's normal flow (a banner, a chip, a row);",
    "  kind \"text\"    - a single line of copy;",
    "  kind \"page\"    - the success state, evidenced by the page's own heading or test id;",
    "  kind \"absent\"  - the state is not implemented; the reason says what the reader sees instead;",
    "  kind \"not-applicable\" - the state cannot exist for this page shape, and the reason says why.",
    "\"data\" records the page shape: \"fetch\" reads something over the network, \"mutation\" submits a form,",
    "\"static\" renders committed copy or a build-time import.",
    "__tests__/fourState.test.js holds this against a live scan: every page file is ledgered and every ledgered",
    "file exists, every evidence string is still in the file, a \"fetch\" page may not declare loading or error",
    "not-applicable, a state that is not retryable has to say why, and the count of \"absent\" states may not grow."
  ],
  "states": [
    "loading",
    "empty",
    "error",
    "success"
  ],
